WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.259
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:16.494
Unit thirty-three: The Future of Work. In this unit, you will discuss changes in work using advanced future forms.

4
00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:18.496
hybrid work.

5
00:00:19.196 --> 00:00:22.600
hybrid work means working partly at home and partly in the office.

6
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.119
Our company adopted hybrid work after 2020.

7
00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:29.228
Your turn. Say: hybrid work.

8
00:00:31.928 --> 00:00:33.056
hybrid work.

9
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.098
digital nomad.

10
00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:39.690
digital nomad means a person who works online while travelling.

11
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.256
Kampot attracts many digital nomads.

12
00:00:42.956 --> 00:00:45.736
Your turn. Say: digital nomad.

13
00:00:48.436 --> 00:00:49.751
digital nomad.

14
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.763
four-day week.

15
00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:56.192
four-day week means a working week of four days instead of five.

16
00:00:56.492 --> 00:00:59.003
Some companies are testing a four-day week.

17
00:00:59.703 --> 00:01:02.308
Your turn. Say: four-day week.

18
00:01:05.008 --> 00:01:06.079
four-day week.

19
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:08.108
upskilling.

20
00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:11.690
upskilling means learning new skills for your current job.

21
00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.709
Upskilling is essential in a changing job market.

22
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.458
Your turn. Say: upskilling.

23
00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:21.251
upskilling.

24
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.553
automation risk.

25
00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:28.017
automation risk means the chance that a job will be done by machines.

26
00:01:28.317 --> 00:01:30.862
Data entry has a high automation risk.

27
00:01:31.562 --> 00:01:34.319
Your turn. Say: automation risk.

28
00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:38.427
automation risk.

29
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:40.824
work-life integration.

30
00:01:41.524 --> 00:01:45.741
work-life integration means combining work and personal life flexibly.

31
00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:48.993
Work-life integration suits parents with young children.

32
00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:52.972
Your turn. Say: work-life integration.

33
00:01:55.672 --> 00:01:57.428
work-life integration.

34
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.383
gig worker.

35
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:03.627
gig worker means a person who does short jobs, often through apps.

36
00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:06.611
Gig workers often have no health insurance.

37
00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:09.824
Your turn. Say: gig worker.

38
00:02:12.524 --> 00:02:13.583
gig worker.

39
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.875
career resilience.

40
00:02:16.575 --> 00:02:20.606
career resilience means the ability to adapt when your career changes.

41
00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.393
Career resilience is a key skill for the future.

42
00:02:24.093 --> 00:02:26.664
Your turn. Say: career resilience.

43
00:02:29.364 --> 00:02:30.923
career resilience.

44
00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.905
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:36.994
What do you think work will look like in 2040?

46
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:40.852
Most office jobs are set to become hybrid work.

47
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:46.112
And many routine jobs are due to disappear because of automation risk.

48
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:50.475
Right. That's why upskilling is about to become essential.

49
00:02:51.783 --> 00:02:53.911
I might become a digital nomad!

50
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:58.017
Then career resilience will be your most important skill.

51
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:02.106
Grammar focus: Advanced future forms.

52
00:03:02.406 --> 00:03:08.323
Be set to means something is expected to happen. Be due to means it is scheduled. Be about to means very soon.

53
00:03:08.623 --> 00:03:13.699
For example: AI is set to transform many jobs, and the meeting is about to begin.

54
00:03:13.999 --> 00:03:16.277
They are common in news and formal English.

55
00:03:16.577 --> 00:03:21.688
These forms are common in news and formal English to describe planned or expected future events.

56
00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:25.301
Now read and listen. Work Without Walls.

57
00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:29.168
Hybrid work is set to become the normal model for office workers.

58
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:33.853
Several countries are due to test a four-day week in the coming years.

59
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.624
Meanwhile, millions of gig workers already earn money through apps.

60
00:03:39.917 --> 00:03:43.298
Jobs with a high automation risk are about to change dramatically.

61
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:49.137
Experts agree that upskilling and career resilience will protect workers.

62
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.940
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.122
A person who works online while travelling is a blank.

64
00:03:56.422 --> 00:04:00.342
A, digital nomad. B, gig worker. C, hybrid work.

65
00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.698
The answer is A: digital nomad.

66
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:10.229
The train is blank arrive at 6 p.m.

67
00:04:10.529 --> 00:04:13.208
A, due to. B, about. C, set.

68
00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:18.740
The answer is A: due to.

69
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.415
Hurry! The film is blank start.

70
00:04:22.715 --> 00:04:25.637
A, due. B, about to. C, set.

71
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.522
The answer is B: about to.

72
00:04:33.017 --> 00:04:35.608
Learning new skills for your current job is blank.

73
00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:40.572
A, upskilling. B, automation risk. C, four-day week.

74
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.386
The answer is A: upskilling.

75
00:04:47.883 --> 00:04:50.858
According to the text, what is set to become normal?

76
00:04:51.158 --> 00:04:55.322
A, hybrid work. B, gig work. C, five-day weeks.

77
00:04:59.317 --> 00:05:01.525
The answer is A: hybrid work.

78
00:05:03.017 --> 00:05:08.203
Now it's your turn to speak. Would you like to work a four-day week or as a digital nomad? Why?

79
00:05:13.503 --> 00:05:19.057
A four-day week sounds ideal. Many companies are set to try it, and I'd have more time for my family.

80
00:05:19.357 --> 00:05:21.299
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:22.283 --> 00:05:26.375
Great work today! You learned eight new words and advanced future forms.

82
00:05:26.675 --> 00:05:30.071
Today's value is good habits. Do good things every day.

83
00:05:30.371 --> 00:05:32.930
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

84
00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:36.370
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

